From 98ff9f3ddc253bf696a50775becf721e515468ef Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Regi2cWorker <regi2c@esp32s3vm.local>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 10:41:56 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] hw/misc/esp32s3_regi2c: model REGI2C analog I2C master +
 SAR2/PWDT sequencer

SEQUENCING-ONLY, FAIL-CLOSED (rev B). Undocumented block
0x6000E000-0x6000E0FF, decoded from the rev0 ROM (esp32s3_rev0_rom.elf)
and MMIO write traces of unmodified Wi-Fi/BLE calibration runs:

- Parallel engine transaction words +0x00/+0x04: BIT24 start, BIT25 busy
  self-clearing after the modeled I2C wire time (APB 80 MHz / +0x58
  divider, 37 bits); func ids 0/1 evidenced, others diagnosed.
- Analog I2C slave register FILE for config storage: writes latch bytes,
  reads return stored state -- the ROM grammar is read-modify-write
  everywhere (rom_chip_i2c_readReg_org, rom_i2c_readReg_Mask), including
  the bootloader early-boot RMWs (slave 0x69 reg 7 = I2C_SAR_ADC
  DTEST/ENT_TSENS/ENCAL_REF). Reset defaults UNKNOWN, modeled 0;
  never-written reads diagnosed once. NOT measurement data.
- SAR2/PWDT sequencer (+0x50/0x5c/0x60, FIFO +0x80..+0x9c) phase-sequenced
  CMD->SAMPLING->idle, armed by the SENS SAR2 force pair
  0x60008830/0x60008834; +0x50[26:24] reports the phase (idle 7).
- TX-DC word +0x4c (command BIT0 starts a timed op).
- SENS_SAR_TCTRL 0x60008850 TSENS dump_out/ready contract.
- FAIL-CLOSED: SAR2 result words, TSENS samples and TX-DC done/flags
  require a measurement provider (QOM link meas-provider, interface
  esp32s3-regi2c-meas-provider). Without one the device reports the exact
  unavailable dependency ONCE and pauses the VM from a bottom half
  (vm_stop(RUN_STATE_PAUSED), never inside a timerlist run); no DONE+0,
  no filler values, no automatic resume. Exploratory fail-open runs of
  rev A are preserved unqualified under
  build-runtime-state/regi2c-2026-10-07/exploratory/.

Effect on fixtures: all sequencing stages complete (boot smoke 3/3; wifi
records through esp_wifi_start enter; ble through esp_bt_controller_enable
enter) and both pause at the first measurement consumption (SAR2/PWDT
conversion #1) with a single precise diagnostic.
